  - >-
    Seven years after bidding farewell to arenas in 2018 — and after sudden,
    severe hearing loss in his left ear while recording 2023’s Seven Psalms
    nearly ended his live career for good — Paul Simon staged an extraordinary
    comeback in acoustically prized theaters. Working alongside audio engineers
    and the Stanford Initiative to Cure Hearing Loss, his team built a bespoke
    low-volume moving-monitor stage setup tailored to his hearing.
  - >-
    The evening unfolded in two distinct acts: first, the uninterrupted live
    debut of his seven-movement acoustic suite Seven Psalms, followed by an
    intimate second set reimagining solo and Simon & Garfunkel classics.
